;; THE FREEZE MANIFEST — what this package was copied from, pinned by digest
;; (rf2-hic-001).
;;
;; rf2-hic-001's whole value is that Wave B can trust one sentence: *the
;; package is the prototype, moved*. A sentence is not a check. This file is
;; the check's data — every donor file the copy read, with the digest it had
;; when it was read — and `scripts/check_freeze.py` beside it is the check.
;;
;; ## What a red run means
;;
;; A red row does NOT mean someone did something wrong. It means the bench
;; tree and the package have diverged, and somebody has to say which one is
;; now right:
;;
;;   - the fix landed in the BENCH tree and the package needs it too — port
;;     it, then re-pin with `python scripts/check_freeze.py --update`;
;;   - the fix landed in the PACKAGE and the bench tree is now the stale copy
;;     — that is expected and permanent from the moment rf2-hic-009 starts
;;     carving the runtime into owned modules, and the honest response is to
;;     retire the row rather than to re-pin it;
;;   - the divergence is nobody's intent — which is exactly the case this
;;     file exists to catch, and it is caught before Wave B builds on it.
;;
;; ## Digests are line-ending normalised
;;
;; `:sha256` is taken over the file's bytes with CRLF collapsed to LF, because
;; the same commit checks out with CRLF on Windows and LF on Mac and Linux. A
;; raw-byte digest would be green on one maintainer's machine and red on
;; another's for a file nobody touched.
;;
;; ## `:whole-file?` false, and why no row carries it today
;;
;; A row whose package file is not a rename-only image of its donor sets
;; `:whole-file?` false, and is then held to its SHAPES instead: every
;; top-level definition the DONOR makes must appear in the package with an
;; identical READER FORM once renames are applied — same tokens, same
;; strings, same docstrings, whitespace and comments set aside. The roster
;; comes from the donor rather than from a list here, so such a row cannot be
;; silently under-pinned.
;;
;; No row carries it as of the second retirement below. The field is contract
;; rather than decoration — `check_freeze.py`'s self-test exercises it in both
;; directions — and the next donor that is copied with a re-wrap will use it.

;; ## The first retirement: `arm1/runtime.cljs` (rf2-hic-009)
;;
;; The header above names the moment this file starts shedding rows, and
;; rf2-hic-009 is it. That bead carved the copied 2,120-line runtime into six
;; owned modules so Wave B's file fences are real files:
;;
;;   impl/collector.cljs   the render context, the cell table, the commit, the
;;                         two read tiers, the read-set entries, the generation
;;                         fence, the two shells and the two mint doors
;;   impl/generation.cljs  the flush generation, the registry epoch, commit-basis
;;   impl/frames.cljs      the one frame-locked memo row per frame id —
;;                         incarnation, captured bundle and ambient dispatch
;;                         coupled — its lazy replacement and the reset door
;;   impl/roots.cljs       the hydration adoption window
;;   impl/evidence.cljs    the dev-only sink seam
;;   impl/inventory.cljs   the retention census, declared and measured
;;
;; There is no longer a package file that is `arm1/runtime.cljs` moved, so its
;; row is RETIRED rather than re-pinned — the third of the header's three
;; responses, and the one it names for exactly this bead. The consequence is
;; stated rather than hidden: **the bench tree's `arm1/runtime.cljs` is no
;; longer digest-pinned by anything.** It goes on running under
;; `:hicasso-bench`, and a fix landing there is now a fix somebody has to port
;; by reading, not by being told.
;;
;; Three rows SURVIVE with `:whole-file? false` newly on them —
;; `arm1/mount.cljs`, `arm1/boundary.cljs` and `arm1/presence.cljs`. Each
;; imported `arm1.runtime` and now imports the module that answers for the vars
;; it used, so each differs from its donor by its `:require` block and by the
;; prose that named the old namespace. Their donors stay pinned, which is the
;; half of the row that still earns its keep.

;; ## The second retirement: everything under `arm1/` (rf2-hic-001)
;;
;; The paragraph directly above did not survive contact with a gate that
;; actually reads the package. It was written against a `check_freeze.py` that
;; hashed each DONOR and then checked only that the package path EXISTED —
;; `:whole-file?` was read and never used, so setting it false cost nothing and
;; those three rows went green without being compared to anything. rf2-hic-001
;; was reopened over exactly that false green (audits #7735 and #7743), and
;; with `:whole-file?` false now meaning "held to shapes", all four remaining
;; `arm1/` rows fail.
;;
;; They fail for a reason that is not a defect, and the evidence says so
;; precisely. Eleven shapes differ across the four rows, and **every one of the
;; eleven differs only in a namespace segment — the var name after the `/` is
;; identical in all eleven, and there are zero non-namespace differences**:
;;
;;   (rt/dispatch!            →  (collector/dispatch!
;;   (rt/sub                  →  (collector/sub
;;   (rt/adopting?)           →  (roots/adopting?)
;;   impl.runtime/mint-view!  →  impl.collector/mint-view!    … and so on
;;
;; That is the split re-pointing call sites at the module that now answers for
;; each var, and it corroborates rf2-hic-009's "0 dropped, 0 duplicated, no
;; behaviour changed" mechanically rather than by reading. What it also shows
;; is that `:renames` — a ONE-TO-ONE table from bench namespace to package
;; namespace — can no longer express these files. `arm1.runtime` became six
;; namespaces, and which one a given call site should name depends on the VAR
;; being called, not on the file. No entry in a one-to-one table can say that.
;;
;; So the rows are stale rather than the code being wrong, and the header's
;; third response applies for the second time: RETIRE, do not re-pin. Retired
;; here are `arm1/boundary.cljs`, `arm1/mount.cljs`, `arm1/presence.cljs` and
;; `arm1/lang.clj`. Seven rows remain, all `front/*`, all whole-file.
;;
;; ## What the second retirement COSTS, stated rather than hidden
;;
;; Retiring a row drops its donor digest along with its package comparison, so
;; the sentence above about donors staying pinned stops being true for these
;; four. Combined with the first retirement, **no file under the bench tree's
;; `arm1/` is pinned by anything any more** — all five are now ported by
;; reading, not by being told.
;;
;; The sharpest loss is `arm1/lang.clj`, and it deserves naming because it is
;; not proportionate to the damage. Only ONE of its three macros re-points:
;; `defview`, whose expansion target moved from `impl.runtime/mint-view!` to
;; `impl.collector/mint-view!`. `hfn` and `defhost` still match their donor
;; exactly. But a row is judged whole — the alternative is a per-shape
;; exemption, which is the one thing this gate must never grow — so retiring it
;; un-pins all three, and the AUTHORING SURFACE, the part of the package a
;; consumer actually writes against, is now the least-checked thing here.
;; Re-pinning that surface by some means other than a donor diff is worth a
;; follow-up bead; it is not something this bead should invent schema for.

{:donor-root "implementation/freehand/test/re_frame/bench/hicasso"

 ;; The namespace rename the copy applied, in full. A reference to a bench
 ;; namespace NOT in this table — a test, a shape, a bench app — was
 ;; deliberately left verbatim in the copied docstrings: it is provenance
 ;; pointing into the frozen tree, and rewriting it would point at a file the
 ;; package does not contain.
 ;;
 ;; ONE further textual change was applied, and it is enumerated here because
 ;; "the package is the prototype, moved" has to survive contact with a reader
 ;; who checks. `scripts/check_thrown_error_messages.py` reaches
 ;; `implementation/*/src` but not the bench tree's `test/`, so six copied
 ;; files met a gate their donors never did — each at the same shared
 ;; `(defn- fail! [id where reason recovery extra] …)` helper. The gate's own
 ;; documentation calls this shape its "computed discriminator" FALSE RED: the
 ;; runtime message does carry the `[:rf.error/…]` token, `id` is simply a
 ;; parameter, so the source cannot show what the message will say. Its
 ;; prescribed remedy is the `rf2:builder-bypass-ok` marker comment, and that
 ;; is what was added — four comment lines above each throw, in
 ;; codec / intent / presence / route-link / runtime / state. No expression
 ;; changed, no complaint text moved, no dependency was added. Making those
 ;; helpers genuinely delegate to `re-frame.error` would change the complaint
 ;; text, which is rf2-hic-021's (the complaint catalogue) to rule on.
 :renames
 {re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.codec      re-frame.hicasso.impl.codec
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.controlled re-frame.hicasso.impl.controlled
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.intent     re-frame.hicasso.impl.intent
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.presence   re-frame.hicasso.impl.presence
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.route-link re-frame.hicasso.impl.route-link
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.slot       re-frame.hicasso.impl.slot
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.front.state      re-frame.hicasso.impl.state
  ;; RETIRED as a single target by rf2-hic-009 — the package side is now
  ;; impl.{collector,generation,frames,roots,evidence,inventory}. Kept in the
  ;; table because the table records what the COPY did, and the copy did this.
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.arm1.runtime     re-frame.hicasso.impl.runtime
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.arm1.boundary    re-frame.hicasso.impl.boundary
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.arm1.mount       re-frame.hicasso.impl.mount
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.arm1.presence    re-frame.hicasso.impl.presence-react
  re-frame.bench.hicasso.arm1.lang        re-frame.hicasso}

 ;; Namespace prefixes no file under `implementation/hicasso/` may IMPORT.
 ;; Prose may name them — a docstring citing the witness that pins a
 ;; behaviour is worth more than a clean grep — but a `:require`,
 ;; `:require-macros` or runtime `require` of one would make the package
 ;; depend on the benchmark tree, which is the dependency this whole file
 ;; exists to prevent.
 :forbidden-import-prefixes ["re-frame.bench." "re-frame.freehand."]

